// The diagnostics/ directory contains debugging and diagnostic utilities,
// not crash handling code. Key files:

// diagnostics/disasm.h - Disassembler for machine code
// diagnostics/disassembler.h - Higher-level disassembler interface
// diagnostics/gdb-jit.h - GDB JIT interface for debugging
// diagnostics/perf-jit.h - Perf JIT profiling interface
// diagnostics/eh-frame.h - Exception handling frame information
// diagnostics/unwinder.h - Stack unwinding utilities
// diagnostics/code-tracer.h - Code tracing utilities
// diagnostics/basic-block-profiler.h - Basic block profiling
// diagnostics/compilation-statistics.h - Compilation statistics
// diagnostics/etw-jit-win.h - ETW (Event Tracing for Windows) JIT logging

// Note: The diagnostics directory does NOT contain crash handling code.
// Crash handling is primarily in:
// - base/logging.h/.cc (CHECK macros, V8_Fatal)
// - base/abort-mode.h/.cc (abort behavior control)
// - base/platform/platform-*.cc (OS::Abort implementations)
// - api/api.cc (FatalProcessOutOfMemory)
// - init/v8.cc (abort mode selection)

// The file src/utils/abort-message.cc mentioned in the task does not exist.
// Error message formatting for crashes is handled in:
// - base/logging.cc (FailureMessage class in V8_Fatal)
// - runtime/runtime-test.cc (abort message printing for testing)
